  "body": "This is particularly useful for users of most SPA-oriented frameworks (e.g. React, Angular), who don't *need* to ID their elements, and where IDing them would cause duplicate IDs to exist in the document (which would complicate things further).\r\n\r\nCurrently, you have to ID *all* labels that don't contain their control. If this could be relaxed with something, that'd be nice. In particular, I'm considering these kinds of pretty common scenarios:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!-- Example 1 -->\r\n<label for=\"foo\">...</label>\r\n<input id=\"foo\">\r\n\r\n<!-- Example 2 -->\r\n<input id=\"foo\">\r\n<label for=\"foo\">...</label>\r\n```\r\n\r\nMaybe adding an attribute (e.g. `forsibling=\"prev|next\"`) that references the nearest sibling labelable in that direction would make this a bit easier to use.",
